    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0086" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg6"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Lord.</hi><anchor n="b" xml:id="d7-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-24"><hi rendition="#italic">May 24,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>You are instructed, at the request of the President of Cuba, to ask the
                    Government of Argentina to permit United States consular officers within its
                    jurisdiction to use their good offices in representation of the interests of
                    Cuba and of its citizens until Cuban consuls shall have been appointed.</p>
                <p>If permission is granted, notify consuls.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d7-f1" n="b" type="source" xml:id="d7-f1-content">
                <p>Same telegram, mutatis mutandis, to all United States diplomatic
                    representatives</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
